  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-deepseek-account",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA **DeepSeek account plugin** for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/sunyuhuirong/deepseek-harness). It adds a wallet button next to Settings in the web GUI sidebar; clicking it shows a balance card for the configured account, and a `deepseek_balance` tool lets the agent query the balance itself.\n\n**Balance display only.** API keys are never stored by this plugin — they stay in the harness Settings under the `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` credential."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Sidebar wallet button + balance popover (with rail/wide sidebar states)\n- `deepseek_balance` tool available to the agent\n- i18n: English + 简体中文"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires DeepSeek Harness (Node `^22.19` or `>=24`, `~/.dsh` profiles).\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from any harness profile",
      "text": "dsh plugin add @deepseek-ai/dsh-deepseek-account --profile web\n```\n\nThen configure the account in Settings (the plugin reads the existing `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` credential; no extra setup)."
    },
    {
      "section": "From source",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm bundle        # build src -> lib\npnpm test          # unit tests\n```\n\nThe plugin is developed inside the harness monorepo (`packages/extensions/deepseek-account`); the standalone repo mirrors the same source with npm-installable dependency ranges. The peer dependencies (client runtime, slots, etc.) are provided by the harness at runtime."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "- **Host half** (`src/index.ts`, `src/balance.ts`): registers the `deepseek_balance` tool, which reads the account credential via the harness credentials service and calls the DeepSeek balance API.\n- **Client half** (`src/client/`): registers into the `settings.triggerExtra` slot (a wallet button next to Settings) and renders the balance card popover."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
